<BaseLayout title="About">
  <article>
    <header class="article-header">
      <h1>About This Blog</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>AI safety and alignment are the defining challenges of our era. As AI systems grow more capable — approaching and potentially exceeding human-level performance across many domains — the question of whether these systems will reliably do what we <em>intend</em> becomes urgent.</p>

      <p>This blog is my personal exploration of these issues. I write about:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI Alignment</strong> — making AI systems pursue the goals we intend, not just the ones we specify</li>
        <li><strong>Safety Research</strong> — RLHF, Constitutional AI, mechanistic interpretability, red-teaming</li>
        <li><strong>Real-World Implications</strong> — how alignment failures show up in deployed systems today</li>
        <li><strong>Frontier Developments</strong> — analysis of new papers, techniques, and debates</li>
      </ul>

      <p>I'm a builder and researcher with 10+ years in AI, four years in the modern generative AI era, and a growing conviction that alignment is the most important unsolved problem we face.</p>

      <p>Read the research. Build safer. Think clearly.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
